### 1. Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login (save the token from response)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Create a post (requires auth - replace TOKEN with your token from login)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "My First Blog Post",
  "content": "This is the content of my first blog post. It's longer than 10 characters!"
}

### 4. List all posts (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/posts

### 5. Get a specific post with comments (replace POST_ID)
GET http://localhost:8080/posts/POST_ID_HERE

### 6. Update a post (requires auth + ownership)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/posts/POST_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "My Updated Blog Post",
  "published": true
}

### 7. Add a comment to a post (requires auth)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts/POST_ID_HERE/comments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "content": "Great post! Thanks for sharing."
}

### 8. Delete a post (requires auth + ownership)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/posts/POST_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### === Error Examples ===

### Validation Error - Title too short
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "Hi",
  "content": "This is the content"
}

### Unauthorized - Missing token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My First Blog Post",
  "content": "This is the content"
}

### Unauthorized - Invalid credentials
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "wrong@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Conflict - Email already exists
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
